IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `tas-ss08-10a-reading-and-commencement`
IMPORT `tas-ss14-18a-repeal-and-expiry`
IMPORT `tas-ss29a-31-units-service-and-notices`
IMPORT `tas-ss47-regulations`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), consolidated version of 26 October 2022 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under a Tasmanian Act or statutory rule (to apply, object, appeal, reply or pay),
-- or who needs to know when something takes effect, asking on which day their period ends and which of their days count.
--
-- Every question takes plain inputs: yes or no, a number, a date, a list of dates, or a choice the layer-1 modules already name.
-- Each input has a @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- Every question calls a layer-1 rule and restates none; no layer-1 module changes to suit this layer.
-- Nothing here is new law.
--
-- Where a question returns a MAYBE value, NOTHING means that the text does not answer the question for the facts given.
-- The Act gives no statutory holidays, no public holidays and no sitting days of its own, so the person supplies the dates (a list), as the layer-1 modules ask.
-- The Act does not give the day on which section 8 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 commenced, so the first question asks for it.
-- A date input that a rule does not read for the facts given may be filled with any date; its @desc says so.

§ `When an Act or an instrument comes into operation and stops operating (ss 9, 14)`

@export On which day does an Act come into operation (s 9)?
GIVEN `the day the Act received Royal Assent` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Act receive Royal Assent?
      `the Act was reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Act reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure?
      `the day the Act was reserved` IS A DATE @desc If the Act was reserved, on which day was it reserved? (If it was not reserved, give any date.)
      `the day the proclamation signifying the Sovereign's assent was published or notified in the Gazette` IS A DATE @desc If the Act was reserved, on which day was the Governor's proclamation of the Sovereign's assent published or notified in the Gazette? (If it was not reserved, give any date.)
      `the day section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act commenced` IS A DATE @desc On which day did section 8 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 commence? (The Act does not say.)
      `the Act shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act itself show an intention that it should come into operation otherwise than as the Act says?
      `the Act provides for commencement on a day or days to be proclaimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act say that it, or a part of it, commences on a day or days to be proclaimed?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an Act come into operation` IS
    `s 9: the day on which an Act as a whole comes into operation` `the day the Act received Royal Assent` `the Act was reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure` `the day the Act was reserved` `the day the proclamation signifying the Sovereign's assent was published or notified in the Gazette` `the day section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act commenced` `the Act shows a contrary intention` `the Act provides for commencement on a day or days to be proclaimed`

@export Is an Act, regulation or other instrument already in operation, or still in operation, at the start or the end of a given day (ss 9(5), 14(2))?
GIVEN `the day it is expressed to commence` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the Act, regulation or other instrument say that it commences, comes into operation or takes effect?
      `the day it is expressed to expire or to remain in force until` IS A DATE @desc On which day does it say that it expires, ceases to operate or remains in force until? (If it says nothing, give a date long after the day you ask about.)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc On which day do you want to know whether it is in operation?
      `I ask about the first moment of that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you ask about the first moment of that day? (Answer no to ask about the last moment of that day.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Act or instrument in operation at the moment` IS
    `s 9(5) and s 14(2): an enactment commencing on a day and expiring on a day is in operation at a moment` `the day it is expressed to commence` `the day it is expressed to expire or to remain in force until` (`Moment in a day` OF `the day I ask about`, (IF `I ask about the first moment of that day` THEN `the first moment of the day` ELSE `the last moment of the day`))

§ `When a right or a liability ends (ss 15, 16, 18A)`

@export Are the old provisions still in force on a given day, while the provisions that replace them have not yet come into operation (s 15(1))?
GIVEN `an Act repeals, wholly or in part, a former Act and substitutes provisions in lieu of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an Act repealed, wholly or in part, a former Act and substituted provisions in lieu of it?
      `the day the substituted provisions come into operation` IS A DATE @desc On which day do the substituted provisions come into operation?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc On which day do you want to know whether the repealed provisions are still in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day` IS
    `s 15(1): the repealed provisions remain in force on the day` `an Act repeals, wholly or in part, a former Act and substitutes provisions in lieu of it` `the day the substituted provisions come into operation` `the day I ask about`

@export May I still start or continue a legal proceeding about a right under an Act that has been repealed or has expired (s 16(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the Act has been repealed, or has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Act, or the enactment, that gave you the right been repealed, or has it expired?
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the repealing Act, or the enactment, expressly provide otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I still bring a legal proceeding after a repeal or expiry` IS
    `s 16(1) and (2) closing words: the investigation, proceeding, remedy or penalty may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed or the enactment had not expired` `the Act has been repealed, or has expired` `the contrary is expressly provided` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment`

@export Am I free from punishment for something I did after a temporary Act expired and before the Act continuing it was assented to (s 18A)?
GIVEN `a Bill for continuing the temporary enactment was introduced and had not been passed when it expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a Bill for continuing the temporary enactment introduced into Parliament, and not yet passed, when the temporary enactment expired?
      `the Bill has received assent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Bill received the Governor's assent (or, if it was reserved, has the Sovereign's assent been proclaimed by the Governor)?
      `the day the temporary enactment expired` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the temporary enactment expire?
      `the day of that assent` IS A DATE @desc On which day was that assent given? (If it has not been given, give any date.)
      `the day I did or failed to do the thing` IS A DATE @desc On which day did you do the thing, or fail to do it?
      `what I did or failed to do was contrary to the temporary enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you did, or failed to do, contrary to a provision of the temporary enactment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I free from punishment between expiry and assent` IS
    `s 18A: the person is not liable to punishment, penalty or forfeiture for the thing done or omitted` `a Bill for continuing the temporary enactment was introduced and had not been passed when it expired` `the Bill has received assent` `the day the temporary enactment expired` `the day of that assent` `the day I did or failed to do the thing` `what I did or failed to do was contrary to the temporary enactment`

§ `Counting my time (s 29)`

-- Sundays are always days that do not count; the person lists the statutory holidays and the public holidays, which the Act does not give.

@export By which day must I act, if the Act gives me a number of days from a given day (s 29(1), (3), (6))?
GIVEN `the day my period runs from` IS A DATE @desc On which day does your period run from (the day of the act or event, or the day given in the Act)?
      `the number of days I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the Act give you?
      `the days that do not count` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the dates, at the end of or within your period, on which there is a statutory holiday or a public holiday where you must act. (Sundays are counted for you.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By which day must I act` IS
    `s 29: the last day for doing an act within a number of days reckoned forwards from` `the day my period runs from` `for` `the number of days I have` `with the excluded days` `the days that do not count`

@export By which day must I act, if the Act gives me a number of calendar months from a given day (ss 29(1), (3), 46)?
GIVEN `the day my period runs from` IS A DATE @desc On which day does your period run from?
      `the number of calendar months I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar months does the Act give you?
      `the days that do not count` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the dates on which there is a statutory holiday or a public holiday where you must act. (Sundays are counted for you.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must I act in calendar months` IS
    `s 29(3)(a) and s 46: the last day on which an act is in due time, a period of calendar months reckoned forwards from` `the day my period runs from` `for` `the number of calendar months I have` `with the excluded days` `the days that do not count`

@export By which day must I act, if the Act gives me a number of years from a given day (s 29(1))?
GIVEN `the day my period runs from` IS A DATE @desc On which day does your period run from?
      `the number of years I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years does the Act give you?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must I act in years` IS
    `s 29(1): the last day of a period of years reckoned forwards from` `the day my period runs from` `for` `the number of years I have`

@export On or before which day must I act, if the Act gives me a number of days, counted backwards from a given day (s 29(1), (3)(b), (6))?
GIVEN `the day my period runs back from` IS A DATE @desc From which day do you count backwards (for example the day of the hearing)?
      `the number of days I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before that day does the Act require you to act?
      `the days that do not count` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the dates on which there is a statutory holiday or a public holiday where you must act. (Sundays are counted for you.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On or before which day must I act, counting backwards` IS
    CONSIDER `s 29(6): the first day of a time not exceeding 6 days reckoned backwards from` `the day my period runs back from` `for` `the number of days I have` `excluding the excluded days` `the days that do not count`
    WHEN JUST d THEN d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 29(3)(b): the day on or before which an act is in due time, a time reckoned backwards ending on` (`s 29(1): the first day of a period of days reckoned backwards from` `the day my period runs back from` `for` `the number of days I have`) `the days that do not count`

@export On which day may I first act, if the Act requires a number of clear days after a given day (s 29(2))?
GIVEN `the given day` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the count start (the day of the act or event)?
      `the number of clear days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear days (or "days at least") does the Act require?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day may I first act after clear days` IS
    `s 29(2): the earliest day on which the purpose may be fulfilled after a number of clear days from` `the given day` `for` `the number of clear days`

@export On which day must I act at the latest, if the Act requires a number of clear days before a given day (s 29(2))?
GIVEN `the given day` IS A DATE @desc On which day is the act or event that the clear days must come before (for example the hearing)?
      `the number of clear days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear days (or "days at least") does the Act require?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day must I act at the latest before clear days` IS
    `s 29(2): the latest day on which the purpose may be fulfilled before a number of clear days from` `the given day` `for` `the number of clear days`

@export Is a given day one that does not count in my period, being a Sunday, a statutory holiday or a public holiday (s 29(3))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to ask about?
      `the days that do not count` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the dates on which there is a statutory holiday or a public holiday where you must act.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day one that does not count` IS
    `s 29(3): a day is an excluded day` `the day I ask about` `the days that do not count`

@export On which day may I file or register, if the last day of my period falls on a day when the office is not open (s 29(4))?
GIVEN `the last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period for filing or registering the document or instrument?
      `the office is open on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office in which you must file or register open on that day?
      `the next ensuing day on which the office is open` IS A DATE @desc What is the next day after that one on which the office is open?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day may I file or register` IS
    `s 29(4): the last day on which a document may be filed or registered` `the last day of my period` `when` `the office is open on that day` `and next open on` `the next ensuing day on which the office is open`

@export On which day is my act in due time, if it is directed to be done on a particular day that is an excluded day (s 29(5))?
GIVEN `the particular day` IS A DATE @desc On which particular day is the act or proceeding directed or allowed to be done?
      `the day is fixed as a particular day and is not the end of a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that day fixed as a particular day, and not as the first or last day of a period or time?
      `the days that do not count` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the dates on which there is a statutory holiday or a public holiday where you must act.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is my act in due time on a particular day` IS
    `s 29(5): the day on which an act directed or allowed to be done on a particular day is in due time` `the particular day` `where` (NOT (`the day is fixed as a particular day and is not the end of a period`)) `the days that do not count`

§ `Being served with a notice or document (ss 29AB, 30, 30A)`

@export Has a notice or other document been served on me in a way that section 29AB allows (s 29AB(1))?
GIVEN `an Act authorizes, requires or permits the notice or document to be served on a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act authorize, require or permit the notice or document to be served on a person?
      `the Act directs it to be served in a particular manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act direct that it be served in a particular manner?
      `the kind of person` IS A `Kind of person to be served` @desc Are you a natural person, or any other person (for example a company)?
      `the way I have chosen` IS A `Way of serving a notice or other document` @desc In what way was the notice or document served on you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` IS
    `s 29AB(1): the notice or document may be served on the person in the way` `an Act authorizes, requires or permits the notice or document to be served on a person` `the Act directs it to be served in a particular manner` `the kind of person` `the way I have chosen`

@export On which day am I taken to have been served with a notice or document that was sent to me by post (s 30(1))?
GIVEN `the sender properly addressed it and posted it as a letter, paying the postage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sender properly address the notice or document to you, post it as a letter, and pay for the postage (before or after posting)?
      `the day the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc On which day would the letter be delivered in the ordinary course of post?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the letter was delivered at some other time?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day am I taken to have been served by post` IS
    `s 30(1): the day service by post is deemed to have been effected` `the sender properly addressed it and posted it as a letter, paying the postage` `and` `the day the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` `where` `the contrary is proved`

@export On which day am I taken to have been served with a notice or document that was sent to me by registered post (s 30(2))?
GIVEN `the sender properly addressed it and posted it as a letter, paying the postage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the sender properly address the notice or document to you, post it as a letter, and pay for the postage (before or after posting)?
      `it was duly registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter duly registered, as the postal regulations provide?
      `it was sent by means of the certified mail service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter sent by means of the certified mail service, as the postal regulations provide?
      `the Act shows a contrary intention about the certified mail service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act that requires the service show an intention that the certified mail service is not to be used?
      `the day the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc On which day would the letter be delivered in the ordinary course of post?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the letter was delivered at some other time?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day am I taken to have been served by registered post` IS
    `s 30(2): the day service by registered post is deemed to have been effected` `the sender properly addressed it and posted it as a letter, paying the postage` `and` `it was duly registered` `or` `it was sent by means of the certified mail service` `unless` `the Act shows a contrary intention about the certified mail service` `with` `the day the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` `where` `the contrary is proved`

@export Can an infringement notice be served on me electronically (s 30A(a))?
GIVEN `the document is an infringement notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an infringement notice?
      `I consent to service electronically` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to being served with the notice electronically?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an infringement notice be served on me electronically` IS
    `s 30A(a): the infringement notice may be served electronically` `the document is an infringement notice` `I consent to service electronically`

@export Am I taken to have been served with an infringement notice that was sent to me electronically (s 30A(b))?
GIVEN `the document is an infringement notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document an infringement notice?
      `it was sent electronically to an address or number provided for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent electronically to an address or number provided for that purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to have been served electronically` IS
    `s 30A(b): the infringement notice is taken to have been served on the intended recipient` `the document is an infringement notice` `it was sent electronically to an address or number provided for that purpose`

§ `When a proclamation or regulation takes effect, and when regulations are void (ss 38A, 47)`

@export On which day does a proclamation or order-in-council that does not fix a commencement day take effect (s 38A(2)(d))?
GIVEN `it says on which day it takes effect, or a period from which that day can be worked out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proclamation, order-in-council or instrument say on which day it takes effect, or give a period from which that day can be worked out?
      `the day it takes effect by its own words` IS A DATE @desc On which day does it take effect by its own words? (If it says nothing, give any date.)
      `the day it is published in the Gazette, or its making is notified there` IS A DATE @desc On which day was it published in the Gazette or, for a statutory rule, was its making notified in the Gazette?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a proclamation or order-in-council take effect` IS
    `s 38A(2)(d): the day an instrument other than one fixing a commencement day takes effect` (IF `it says on which day it takes effect, or a period from which that day can be worked out` THEN JUST `the day it takes effect by its own words` ELSE NOTHING) `after` `the day it is published in the Gazette, or its making is notified there`

@export On which day do regulations made under an Act take effect (s 47(3)(d))?
GIVEN `they say on which day they take effect, or give a period from which that day can be worked out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations say on which day they take effect, or give a period from which that day can be worked out?
      `the day they take effect by their own words` IS A DATE @desc On which day do they take effect by their own words? (If they say nothing, give any date.)
      `the day they are published in the Gazette, or their making is notified there` IS A DATE @desc On which day were the regulations published in the Gazette or, if they are statutory rules, was their making notified in the Gazette?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day do regulations take effect` IS
    `s 47(3)(d): the day the regulations take effect` (IF `they say on which day they take effect, or give a period from which that day can be worked out` THEN JUST `the day they take effect by their own words` ELSE NOTHING) `the day they are published in the Gazette, or their making is notified there`

@export Are the regulations that affect me void because they were not published or notified in the Gazette in time, or take effect too early (s 47(3A))?
GIVEN `the day the regulations were made` IS A DATE @desc On which day were the regulations made?
      `they have been published, or their making has been notified, in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the regulations been published in the Gazette or, if they are statutory rules, has their making been notified in the Gazette? (Answer no only if that has not happened and the 21 days after the day they were made have run out.)
      `the day they were published or their making was notified` IS A DATE @desc On which day was that? (If it has not happened, give any date.)
      `the day the regulations say they take effect` IS A DATE @desc On which day do the regulations say they take effect?
      `their rights or privileges would be prejudiced if they took effect before publication or notification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the regulations take effect before they were published or notified, would the rights or privileges of a person other than the Crown in right of the State, or an agency of the State, existing at that date be prejudiced?
      `liabilities or obligations would be imposed if they took effect before publication or notification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the regulations take effect before they were published or notified, would liabilities or obligations be imposed on a person other than the Crown in right of the State, or an agency of the State, for anything done or omitted on or before that date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the regulations void` IS
    `s 47(3A): the regulations are void` `the day the regulations were made` (IF `they have been published, or their making has been notified, in the Gazette` THEN JUST `the day they were published or their making was notified` ELSE NOTHING) `the day the regulations say they take effect` `their rights or privileges would be prejudiced if they took effect before publication or notification` `liabilities or obligations would be imposed if they took effect before publication or notification`
